            'Theravada (School of the Elders) is the oldest surviving branch of Buddhism, dominant in Sri Lanka, Myanmar, Thailand, Cambodia, and Laos. It strictly follows the original Pali Canon (Tripitaka) and emphasizes individual liberation through monastic discipline, meditation, and wisdom. It regards the historical Buddha as a human teacher rather than a divine being, and holds that only monks can attain Nirvana in the current life.',
