          question: 'Who was Chandragupta Maurya?',
          answer:
            'Chandragupta Maurya (r. 321–297 BCE) was the founder of the Mauryan Empire, India\'s first pan-Indian empire. With the guidance of his minister Kautilya (Chanakya), he overthrew the Nanda dynasty, defeated Seleucus I Nicator (winning territories up to modern Afghanistan), and unified most of the Indian subcontinent. He abdicated in favor of his son Bindusara and became a Jain monk, eventually dying by ritual fasting (Sallekhana) at Shravanabelagola.',
